## What Rockstar says now

Rockstar’s Newswire post [Grand Theft Auto VI Now Available](https://www.rockstargames.com/newswire/article/39akk424a9oo53/grand-theft-auto-vi-now-available), dated 19 November 2026, says: “Today we are proud to announce that Grand Theft Auto VI is now available worldwide for PlayStation 5 and XBOX Series X|S.”

[Rockstar’s GTA VI page](https://www.rockstargames.com/VI), rechecked on 23 November 2026 (UTC), no longer says “Coming November 19.” It now shows **Out Now** and **Now Available** with a **Buy Now** button. It lists PlayStation 5 and Xbox Series X|S, and it still labels PlayStation 5 as the platform the game plays best on. The page does not list a PC version or a PC date.

This is a separate game from Grand Theft Auto V Enhanced, which is a released PC game. The Enhanced edition has its own [Steam listing](/apps/gta-v-enhanced).

## Platforms, from official sources

| Platform | What the official sources say |
| --- | --- |
| PlayStation 5 | Named in Rockstar’s 19 November 2026 launch post and on the GTA VI page, which labels it the platform the game plays best on. |
| Xbox Series X\|S | Named in Rockstar’s 19 November 2026 launch post and on the GTA VI page. [Xbox Wire’s 10 November 2026 post](https://news.xbox.com/en-us/2026/11/10/grand-theft-auto-6-comes-to-xbox-cloud-gaming-november-19/) said Xbox Series X and Xbox Series S play the game natively. |
| Xbox One | Not a native platform on Rockstar’s page. The same Xbox Wire post said the game would be playable from day one through Xbox Cloud Gaming on Xbox One and Xbox Series X\|S, starting at 1am ET on November 19, using Xbox Series S graphics settings when streamed. |
| PC | Not listed on Rockstar’s GTA VI page or in the launch post. No PC date has been announced on those pages. |

Xbox Wire’s post also said that Grand Theft Auto VI must be purchased separately, and that cloud gaming availability, purchasing options, supported devices, and features may vary by market and device. On 19 November 2026, Xbox Wire published [Grand Theft Auto VI is Out Now](https://news.xbox.com/en-us/2026/11/19/grand-theft-auto-vi-is-out-now/). The text of that post available during this check gave no further platform or cloud details, so the cloud details above are what Microsoft announced before release.

## How launch day worked

The game launched on 19 November 2026. Before launch, [PlayStation’s 10 November 2026 post](https://blog.playstation.com/2026/11/10/pre-load-grand-theft-auto-vi-on-ps5-starting-today/) said the PS5 version would unlock at midnight local time country by country, starting in New Zealand. Rockstar’s [Pre-Load Grand Theft Auto VI Now](https://www.rockstargames.com/newswire/article/89834o94713o21/pre-load-grand-theft-auto-vi-now) post, also dated 10 November 2026, opened pre-loading for digital pre-orders, and code-in-box buyers could start once they redeemed their code. Now that the game is out, pre-loading no longer applies. Buying the game gets you a normal download.

Rockstar publishes a [platforms and editions support article](https://support.rockstargames.com/articles/4QfG4FmZCf5W1gS8jy4UVT/grand-theft-auto-vi-platform-editions-and-versions) for questions about physical editions and retail codes. Retail stock and shipping depend on the store.

## Timeline

- **6 November 2025:** Rockstar moved the release to 19 November 2026 ([Newswire](https://www.rockstargames.com/newswire/article/ak3ak31a49a221/grand-theft-auto-vi-is-now-set-to-launch-november-19-2026)).
- **15 October 2026:** Rockstar released the [launch trailer](https://www.rockstargames.com/VI/launch-trailer).
- **10 November 2026:** Pre-loading opened on PlayStation 5 and Xbox Series X|S.
- **19 November 2026:** Rockstar announced the game is available worldwide on PlayStation 5 and Xbox Series X|S. Xbox Wire published its own “Out Now” post the same day.

## What this page does not claim

This page does not give a PC release date, because Rockstar has not published one on the pages checked here. It does not quote a download size, because none of the official pages checked gives a gigabyte figure.

This is a dated editorial snapshot of official announcements. It is not a review, a hands-on impression, or a performance comparison. GameNews is not affiliated with Rockstar. For anything newer, go to Rockstar’s page rather than this recap.
